1. She is British and has maintained her British identity while living in Japan. (Verbatim: "I was still British while I was away... there's no cure for that")  
2. She spent the entire month of July in Japan. (Verbatim: "I have been in Japan for pretty much the whole of July")  
3. She has a fluffy dog who was ill shortly after she left for Japan. (Verbatim: "After I left for Japan, she got a bit ill")  
4. She has a dog toy shaped like Japan that squeaks and is her dog’s favorite toy. (Verbatim: "It's literally like the shape of Japan, the island shape... it squeaks")  
5. She has a background in choir singing, though her voice is described as soft. (Verbatim: "I was a choir girl. My issue is my singing voice is a bit on the soft side")  
6. She is working on creating music and has been recording songs. (Verbatim: "I actually spent some of today doing some recording. Yeah, I sing.")  
7. She struggles with feeling rusty after being away from her channel for a month. (Verbatim: "I'm rusty, I'm, I'm, I'm, I'm rusty!")  
8. She has a habit of going on tangents and acknowledges she has a large inventory of them. (Verbatim: "I haven't cured myself of any tangents... I've stocked my tangent inventory with even more tangents")  
9. She has been actively improving her Japanese language skills daily during her time in Japan. (Verbatim: "In Japan, I got like nihongojozu'd every, every single, like, day, every single day")  
10. She is passionate about sharing stories, pictures, and figurines from her time in Japan. (Verbatim: "I have a lot of stories to tell you, a lot of pictures to show you, a lot of figurines to show you") [end of text]



1. She recently returned from an almost month-long trip to Japan. (Verbatim: "I've just come back from my almost month-long trip to Japan")
2. She identifies as British. (Verbatim: "I'm british so i don't mind queues")
3. She has visited Disney Sea in Japan with a friend named Lily. (Verbatim: "when I went to Disney Sea with Lily")
4. She is capable of speaking some Japanese, though not fluently. (Verbatim: "I'd say that i nihongo don't")
5. She has experienced being approached by strangers in Japan who attempted to flirt with her. (Verbatim: "some guys did try to speak to me but I I didn't register it")
6. She finds long queues physically and emotionally taxing, especially in extreme heat. (Verbatim: "it was a tight that was that was definitely the tiniest restaurant i've ever been to um but like so many people were queued up for it as well")
7. She dislikes people cutting queues, which she found upsetting. (Verbatim: "what was upsetting was when when people cut the queue that is truly upsetting")
8. She was surprised by the level of customer service aggression upon returning to England. (Verbatim: "my goodness she was uh uh what's the word um angry i think i think angry")
9. She observed that Japanese customer service is consistently polite and friendly. (Verbatim: "all the customer service that i experienced there was very very kind very happy")
10. She noticed a cultural difference in public behavior, such as avoiding loud talking on public transport. (Verbatim: "don't talk on um public transport be like you know feel like extremely polite that kind of thing") [end of text]



1. She is not an AI and considers herself a real person. (Verbatim: "No i'm not an ai i'm real")  
