4. She plans to see her mother, referred to as "mama elia," the next day. (Verbatim: "i'm gonna see her tomorrow and see what's going on and what i've missed")  
5. She is currently experiencing lightheadedness, which she suspects may be due to consuming a can of jet (likely a beverage). (Verbatim: "i'm assuming the lightheadedness is from is from this can jet like give you lightheadedness")  
6. She values self-care and is trying to look after herself, influenced by encouragement from her community. (Verbatim: "i'm trying to look after myself um so i hope that even while i've been away you've all been looking after yourselves")  
7. She has a strong emotional connection to her community and feels deeply grateful for their support after her break. (Verbatim: "i really really really really really really am i'm very like i mean my bar of like it was just you know just being here so much means so much to me")  
8. She expresses affection for her community using phrases like "I wanna hug you" and "I missed you." (Verbatim: "i wanna hug you damn it thank you")  
9. She has a fondness for mangoes, as she wants to smell like them after showering. (Verbatim: "i want to smell like mangoes yeah")  
10. She refers to her fans as "Stananas" and believes they deserve love and recognition. (Verbatim: "no stananas are here stananas are thing and deserve love okay") [end of text]



1. She visited Japan and bought merchandise from the Nintendo Store and Pokémon Center. (Verbatim: "I went to the Nintendo store. And I went to the Pokemon Center.")
2. She brought back Pokémon-themed tea and other types of tea from Japan. (Verbatim: "I got myself some Pokemon tea. Because that's clearly the type of tea you bring back from Japan.")
3. She struggled with speaking Japanese during her trip and felt embarrassed by misunderstandings. (Verbatim: "hi and i was like what the heck did i just say yes to i hope it's something not bad which turned out to be sometimes was bad actually")
4. She had an awkward experience at a maid cafe in Japan where no staff spoke English. (Verbatim: "accidentally going to that his desk maid cafe bar that was awkward that was an extremely awkward experience")
5. She values making people happy and sees her VTubing as a way to bring joy to others. (Verbatim: "my super super super super super goal is to make people happy")
6. She has a strong emotional connection to her audience, especially those who may have had difficult experiences. (Verbatim: "i picture someone out there that's like past little tiny back in school um elia that um didn't have the bestest time")
7. She feels she lost some of her British accent after spending time in Japan. (Verbatim: "Did Japan change my accent? Did it? Oh no. Did I lose? Did I lose some Britishness?")
8. She drinks English breakfast tea daily and maintained this habit while in Japan. (Verbatim: "I still had tea. I managed to find English breakfast tea.")
9. She enjoys eating crepes, particularly a creme brulee ice cream crepe. (Verbatim: "I did try the crepe I did I did I had a heck of delicious crepe it was it was it was so good oh my goodness")
10. She bought biscuits primarily due to their cute packaging. (Verbatim: "mostly because they come in the cute packaging so i am a sucker for that so i bought it") [end of text]



1. She has a dog named Nugget. (Verbatim: "my dog looks at me and is like sayonara walks out and i'm like yo come back nugget")
2. She has a diagnosed case of agoraphobia. (Verbatim: "i have agoraphobia um so i have like an official diagnosis from a doctor")
3. She struggled with agoraphobia before and received professional help prior to the pandemic. (Verbatim: "i had a lot of help with it with with like um a doctor person pre-covid before the whole lockdown thing")
4. She experienced a significant setback when lockdown forced her back into isolation despite progress in overcoming her agoraphobia. (Verbatim: "then i was told by the world to go back to being a shut in because of lockdown and irony hurt like")
5. She found Japan’s crowd management less stressful than expected due to orderly pedestrian flow. (Verbatim: "in japan it's like natural for people to have some kind of order with their crowds so they naturally will go in either one direction or the other")
6. She prefers crows and sparrows over seagulls. (Verbatim: "i prefer crows and sparrows to to seagulls")
7. She finds seagulls in England intimidating and dangerous due to their tendency to steal food. (Verbatim: "seagulls are scary if you've ever come to england and you see a sign that says watch out for the seagulls")
8. She has severe motion sickness, which affects her ability to use her phone or look out the window while traveling. (Verbatim: "i get travel sick so i normally look out the window i can't look out the window it's like i'm busy and it's in it's underground")
9. She has difficulty with roller coasters and other motion-based rides due to motion sickness. (Verbatim: "i tried to be brave okay i tried i tried um some scary rides i did i really tried")
10. She has a strong aversion to walking and eating in public, especially in England, due to seagull threats. (Verbatim: "i don't like walking and eating one issue i did have though with walking and eating was i bought myself ice cream") [end of text]



1. She climbed Mount Fuji during a trip to Japan. (Verbatim: "I climbed Mount Fuji during my trip I know shock right I did I did a real outdoorsy a true outdoor activity I climbed the mountain I did it I did it I got a stick to show you as well to prove it")
2. She attempted to reach the summit for the sunrise, starting her climb at midnight. (Verbatim: "I left the hut at like midnight so basically I climbed in the day stayed at this hut... continued my climb in the night to get there for the rising sun")
3. She experienced severe weather conditions while climbing, including 60–70 km/h winds, heavy rain, and freezing temperatures. (Verbatim: "I woke up to the sound of wind... 60 70 kilometer per hour winds outside along with tons of rain and a storm and it was freezing")
4. She struggled with visibility due to thick fog, describing it as "like a video game with no maps loaded" and "render distance set to absolute minimum." (Verbatim: "it was like okay the way i thought of it was imagine you're playing a video game but like none of the maps loaded around you")
5. She successfully resisted the urge to throw up during a motion sickness-inducing experience. (Verbatim: "my only thought during that entire ride okay while my eyes were closed was don't throw up don't don't you dare throw up Elliot don't throw up")
6. She consumed five canned hot chocolates at the summit to warm herself after being extremely cold and tired. (Verbatim: "I ordered myself five hot chocolates all for me... I was so cold I was like I'm gonna use these these hot chocolates to to warm my body")
7. She was discouraged by a warning sign advising against continuing the climb due to dangerous weather, but chose to ignore it. (Verbatim: "the weather condition is really really really bad... we advise you wait until past sunrise to climb when the weather conditions are better")
8. She attempted to visit the crater of Mount Fuji but was physically blocked by strong wind, which she compared to an "invisible barrier" in a video game. (Verbatim: "it felt like one of those invisible barriers in games where you try and get past this certain area and the game is just like absolutely not")
9. She is currently in a pre-debut phase and has not yet released her final VTuber model. (Verbatim: "this is a temp model... I'm just waiting I'm waiting I'm waiting")
10. She plans to create comedy skits featuring herself and another VTuber named Eleanor in the future. (Verbatim: "I'd like to do shorts where it's more like little comedy skit kind of things which should be like between me and eleanor would also be there and yeah that kind of thing") [end of text]



