3. She tried high-quality wagyu beef during her trip to Japan and found it exceptionally delicious. (Verbatim: "i can confirm i did try wagyu like the nicest wagyu i could find um it was so nice so yummy it was so")
4. She has difficulty reading Japanese text and relies on Google Translate, which often fails to provide accurate translations. (Verbatim: "i tried to use google translate um on these little labels but it didn't work")
5. She owns a high-quality Japanese kitchen knife that she treats with care and intends to maintain properly. (Verbatim: "now i have my machete and my japanese knife not sure i still have no purpose for the machete")
6. She has a habit of not taking photos of food when it's especially delicious, often eating it before remembering to document it. (Verbatim: "i'm not in the habit of taking photos so i'll like eat it and be like wait a second")
